<TextPage
  title="Privacy Policy — SproutChores"
  description="How SproutChores handles your data: privacy-friendly analytics with consent, a browser-only chart generator that sends us nothing, and your rights under GDPR and CCPA."
  h1="Privacy Policy"
>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: 8 June 2026</p>

  <p>
    SproutChores ("we", "us") respects your privacy. This policy explains what we do — and
    deliberately don't — collect when you use <strong>sproutchores.com</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Our chore-chart generator runs <strong>entirely in your browser</strong>. Names, ages, and chores you type are <strong>never sent to or stored by us</strong>.</li>
    <li>We use <strong>Google Analytics</strong> to understand which pages help families — but only after you <strong>accept analytics</strong> in our cookie banner. Decline and no analytics cookies are set.</li>
    <li>We don't sell your data, and we don't run advertising or affiliate tracking at this time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Information you provide:</strong> none is required to use the site. If you email us, we
    receive your email address and message so we can reply.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Chart generator inputs:</strong> any name, age, or chores you enter are processed locally
    in your browser to render and print your chart. This information is not transmitted to our servers
    (we don't run an application server) and is not stored by us.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Analytics (with consent):</strong> if you accept analytics, Google Analytics 4 sets
    cookies and collects standard, aggregated usage data — pages viewed, approximate region, device
    type, and how you arrived. We use it only to improve the site. We use Google Consent Mode, so
    until you accept, Google does not store analytics cookies on your device.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    We set no non-essential cookies unless you accept analytics. If you accept, Google Analytics
    cookies are used to measure usage. You can change your mind any time by clearing this site's
    cookies and local storage in your browser, which will bring back the consent banner.
  </p>

  <h2>Third parties</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> (Google LLC) — analytics, only after consent. See Google's <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">privacy policy</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> and <strong>GitHub Pages</strong> — DNS and static hosting; they may process standard server/request logs to deliver the site securely.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    SproutChores is intended for <strong>parents and caregivers</strong>, not for children. We do not
    knowingly collect personal information from children under 13 (or the equivalent age in your
    region). The chart generator does not transmit any information a child or parent types.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights (GDPR / UK GDPR / CCPA)</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, or delete personal data
    we hold, to object to processing, or to opt out of "sale" of personal information. Because we
    don't collect personal data beyond what you email us — and analytics is consent-based and
    aggregated — these requests are usually simple. To exercise any right, email
    <a href="mailto:hello@sproutchores.com">hello@sproutchores.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We'll update this page if our practices change (for example, if we add advertising or affiliate
    links) and revise the date above.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy? Email <a href="mailto:hello@sproutchores.com">hello@sproutchores.com</a>.</p>
</TextPage>
